In the measured H10 configuration, NeST's TX/RX costs are 248.44/403.99 ms, versus 215.29/366.42 ms for WHOLE; totals are 652.43 ms for NeST and 39.17 ms for SwinJSCC (S7). H10 shares U10's MCS and ceilings but uses earlier directories (S1.3). Compiled Ada's 3.064-s total is paired with its own 32-source quality (S7.4--S7.5).

